<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    DroidVM's entitlements.

    DROIDVM'S OWN FILE. The identity is DroidVM's; only the *set* of entitlements is informed
    by what the runtime needs, which is recorded in docs/component-inventory.md.

    Only two are here, and each is load-bearing:

      get-task-allow
          The runtime cannot obtain executable memory without a debugger attached, and a
          debugger cannot attach without this. This is also one of the two independent
          reasons DroidVM can never ship on the App Store -- App Review does not permit it,
          which is a licensing-and-distribution fact, not a technical one that might be
          engineered away.

      increased-memory-limit
          A guest running Android needs far more memory than a default app is allowed. Without
          this the process is killed with SIGKILL -- no handler, no crash log -- which is why
          MemoryPressureManager watches available-before-kill rather than total usage.

    Neither is applied to the unsigned IPA: scripts/package_ipa.sh builds with
    CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO, so entitlements are not embedded, and the installer re-signs with
    its own. They are here so the signed path is correct when there is one.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>get-task-allow</key>
    <true/>

    <key>com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
